have to be updated in a millisecond to be
able to see it.

00:50:56.630 --> 00:50:58.020
Otherwise your model will divert.

00:50:58.020 --> 00:50:59.340
I wasn't even saying simulate.

00:50:59.340 --> 00:51:02.250
I'm saying build another biological object.

00:51:02.250 --> 00:51:04.810
Oh that's easy Brazil we know how to do that.

00:51:04.810 --> 00:51:06.150
It's very simple.

00:51:06.150 --> 00:51:09.530
You know so the real question is: is that
it?

00:51:09.530 --> 00:51:10.900
Maybe you could make a President.

00:51:10.900 --> 00:51:12.570
Yeah we can make it here.

00:51:12.570 --> 00:51:13.570
Here.

00:51:13.570 --> 00:51:14.570
There, oh there?

00:51:14.570 --> 00:51:16.350
There I don't know.

00:51:16.350 --> 00:51:23.310
So, so, so to what extent is the history vital
to the function?

00:51:23.310 --> 00:51:26.480
Well I think the evolutionary history is pivotal,
of course.

00:51:26.480 --> 00:51:31.850
We are, we are, we are, our brains are reflecting
the evolutionary history of our species is

00:51:31.850 --> 00:51:33.240
millions of years.

00:51:33.240 --> 00:51:36.390
But we also have the ontogeny of this brain.

00:51:36.390 --> 00:51:41.500
And the life, the unique life, of individual
