01:04:18.630 --> 01:04:24.530
Because I start to think OK we are building
these robots to make burgers to clean floors,

01:04:24.530 --> 01:04:26.670
to do you know this thing.

01:04:26.670 --> 01:04:30.870
But we are not stopping to think what it would
mean to have 60 percent unemployment around

01:04:30.870 --> 01:04:31.870
the world.

01:04:31.870 --> 01:04:34.970
These are questions that we need to bring
as scientists, you know.

01:04:34.970 --> 01:04:41.411
As I said, I love technology and I find that
it can be for the betterment of mankind, many

01:04:41.411 --> 01:04:46.220
things that we're developing today, but some
of these issues have to be brought to society,

01:04:46.220 --> 01:04:48.400
because society has to wait on them.

01:04:48.400 --> 01:04:55.590
They have to think about what it means to
replace all these jobs, you know, in 20 years.

01:04:55.590 --> 01:05:00.410
There's also the large-there's also the question
more generally of whether a purely physicalist

01:05:00.410 --> 01:05:05.210
